    markdown: "# Terms of Service\n\nLast updated: 21 October 2026\n\nThese terms cover your use of the Lately app and service. By creating an account or using Lately, you agree to them.\n\n## What Lately is\n\nLately is a personal tool for saving Instagram reels you want to come back to. You share or paste a reel's link, optionally add a note, and Lately makes a searchable card from the reel's public content.\n\n## Your account\n\n- You need an account to use Lately. Keep your sign-in method (your email inbox or Google account) secure; you are responsible for activity on your account.\n- You must be at least 13 years old to use Lately.\n- You can delete your account at any time from Account and Settings in the app.\n\n## Your content\n\n- Your notes, stacks and settings belong to you. You give Lately permission to store and process them only to run the service for you, as described in the Privacy Policy.\n- The reels you save belong to their creators. Lately stores the link and a card derived from the reel's public content for your personal reference. It does not re-publish reels, and saving a reel does not give you any rights to it.\n- The cards are generated automatically and can be wrong or incomplete. Check important details (addresses, prices, opening hours, instructions) at the source.\n\n## Acceptable use\n\nDo not use Lately to:\n\n- break the law or the rights of others, including creators' rights;\n- try to access other people's accounts or data;\n- overload, probe or disrupt the service, or automate saves beyond normal personal use;\n- resell or redistribute the service or the cards it generates.\n\n## Plans and limits\n\nThe free plan includes a monthly number of saves, shown in the app. We may change the free plan's limits. If we lower them, we will tell you in the app before the change takes effect.\n\n## Lately Pro subscriptions\n\n- **What Pro includes.** Lately Pro removes the free plan's monthly save limit. Everything else in Lately works the same on both plans.\n- **Price and billing.** Pro is sold as a monthly or yearly subscription through Google Play. The price, currency and billing period are shown in the app and on Google Play's purchase screen before you confirm. Google Play charges the payment method on your Google account, and Google Play's terms apply to the payment.\n- **Free trial.** The yearly plan includes a 7-day free trial for new subscribers (Google accounts that have not had Lately Pro before). Unless you cancel before the trial ends, Google Play charges the yearly price when it ends.\n- **Automatic renewal.** A subscription renews automatically at the end of each month or year until you cancel. If the price changes, Google Play tells you before the new price applies to your subscription.\n- **Canceling.** You can cancel at any time in Google Play > Subscriptions, or from Manage subscription in the app. Canceling stops future renewals, and you keep Pro until the end of the period you have paid for. Uninstalling the app or deleting your Lately account does not cancel the subscription.\n- **Refunds.** Payments are handled by Google Play, and refunds follow Google Play's refund policies. You can ask Google Play for a refund or contact us. If a refund ends your subscription, Pro ends with it.\n- **Your account.** Pro is linked to the Lately account you were signed in to when you subscribed. After switching phones, sign in to the same account; if Pro does not show, use Restore purchases.\n\n## Service changes and availability\n\nLately is provided as is and may change, pause or stop features. We aim to keep it running reliably but cannot promise it will always be available or error-free. Instagram may change how reels can be read, which can make some cards incomplete.\n\n## Ending use\n\nYou can stop using Lately and delete your account at any time. Deleting your account does not cancel a Google Play subscription, so cancel it in Google Play first. We may suspend or close accounts that break these terms. When an account is closed, its data is deleted as described in the Privacy Policy.\n\n## Liability\n\nTo the extent the law allows, Lately is not liable for indirect or consequential losses, or for losses caused by relying on automatically generated cards. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under consumer law that cannot be limited.\n\n## Changes to these terms\n\nIf these terms change, the new version will be shown in the app with a new \"Last updated\" date. Continuing to use Lately after a change means you accept the new terms.\n\n## Contact\n\nQuestions about these terms: write to the support email shown on Lately's Google Play listing.\n",
